  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "IMPOWER reduces axis angles with Excel's 66-bit pi (leaving residue on i^2) and rejects |angle| > 2^27 - 1",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 build 20527, IMPOWER(inumber, number) returns #NUM! for 0^0 or negative powers of 0, returns \"0\" if |z|^number underflows to 0 (before checking the angle bound), and otherwise rejects |atan2(im, re) * number| > 134,217,727 (2^27 - 1) with #NUM!. On the real or imaginary axes (re = 0 or im = 0), it uses Excel's 66-bit pi circular reduction for sin/cos(angle), so IMPOWER(\"i\", 2) returns \"-1+1.22514845490862E-16i\" instead of \"-1\". All 2,735 full-bank IMPOWER rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence readings/excel-20527/bank2-answers-impower-more.json and bank2-answers-impower-scalar.json (Excel 16.0 build 20527); 2,735/2,735 full-bank rows match.",
